{
  "description": "Replacing a room window's newest page (relay answer after a store open, subscribe refresh, reconnect). Shared by desktop (channelWindowStore.ts) and mobile (channel_window.dart). Rules: docs/message-sync.md#opening-at-a-position. Rows are [id, created_at] of top-level kind 9 messages in relay order. `current` lists the retained pages oldest-last; page 0 starts at null and each next page starts at the previous page's end cursor. A page's end cursor is its last row when `more`, else null. `aux` entries are [id, target] reactions (kind 7). `threads` maps a page row to the created_at of the thread summary it carries. `live_summaries` are roots holding a live thread summary created at 1. `then_older` is an older page appended from the tail cursor after the replace. Cursors are [created_at, id].",
